#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-scheduling-your-new-code-to-run-intermittently.rst:5
#: c3e2255ffa7141bcb9a7101c4ed4eb0f
msgid "Scheduling Code to Run Intermittently"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-scheduling-your-new-code-to-run-intermittently.rst:7
#: 43c731d0bd4947fd866e9d777540f490
msgid "This page describes how you can schedule some new piece of code you have written to run intermittently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-scheduling-your-new-code-to-run-intermittently.rst:11
#: 1092aebe50fb4bb39a24a8de4852f6b3
msgid "Running your code with the scheduler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-scheduling-your-new-code-to-run-intermittently.rst:13
#: 1fd129bb11b54728922033ba7c5fc78c
msgid "The most flexible way to run your code at a given interval is to use the scheduler.  This can be done by adding your new function to the `scheduler_tasks <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Copter.cpp#L91>`__ array in `Copter.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Copter.cpp>`__. Note that there are actually two task lists, `the upper list <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Copter.cpp#L788>`__ is for high speed CPUs (i.e. Pixhawk) and the `lower list <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Copter.cpp#L856>`__ is for slow CPUs (i.e. APM2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-scheduling-your-new-code-to-run-intermittently.rst:22
#: 2ed8a29102ef4237843b3fae6b75ebf0
msgid "Adding a task is fairly simple, just create a new row in the list (higher in the list means high priority).  The first column holds the function name, the 2nd is a number of 2.5ms units (or 10ms units in case of APM2).  So if you wanted the function executed at 400Hz this column would contain \"1\", if you wanted 50Hz it would contain \"8\".  The final column holds the number of microseconds (i.e. millions of a second) the function is expected to take.  This helps the scheduler guess whether or not there is enough time to run your function before the main loop starts the next iteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-scheduling-your-new-code-to-run-intermittently.rst:60
#: 0de738b50c2649be862635f4f7a50f6b
msgid "Running your code as part of one of the loops"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-scheduling-your-new-code-to-run-intermittently.rst:62
#: c1261306a2314edcb09375d8dd960d63
msgid "Instead of creating a new entry in the scheduler task list, you can add your function to one of the existing timed loops.  There is no real advantage to this approach over the above approach except in the case of the fast-loop.  Adding your function to the fast-loop will mean that it runs at the highest possible priority (i.e. it is nearly 100% guaranteed to run at 400Hz)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-scheduling-your-new-code-to-run-intermittently.rst:69
#: 54c4b13a1ff54a779be730215e6dc14b
msgid "`fast_loop <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Copter.cpp#L229>`__ : runs at 100Hz on APM2, 400Hz on Pixhawk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-scheduling-your-new-code-to-run-intermittently.rst:71
#: 11c68e77037645eab856e604057f7d71
msgid "`fifty_hz_loop <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Copter.cpp#L370>`__ : runs at 50Hz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-scheduling-your-new-code-to-run-intermittently.rst:73
#: 4fc93ca4dea34c888f7c1f527bdfc740
msgid "`ten_hz_logging_loop <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Copter.cpp#L333>`__: runs at 10Hz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-scheduling-your-new-code-to-run-intermittently.rst:75
#: d8267187bbb94f5c9a93a762df624085
msgid "`three_hz_loop <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Copter.cpp#L398>`__: runs at 3.3Hz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-scheduling-your-new-code-to-run-intermittently.rst:77
#: c1c83dc3c7684f318d4174ed5c8da8f4
msgid "`one_hz_loop <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Copter.cpp#L417>`__ : runs at 1Hz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-scheduling-your-new-code-to-run-intermittently.rst:80
#: fde50bca2f014864b0538859c76f4b0b
msgid "So for example if you want your new code to run at 10Hz you could add it to one of the case statements in the `ten_hz_logging_loop() <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Copter.cpp#L333>`__ function found in `Copter.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Copter.cpp>`__."
msgstr ""
